IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg9-x-winding-up`

-- Tests of dg9-x-winding-up.l4 (8 Del. C. sections 278 to 285).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text, beside the assertion, before the run.
-- The wrappers `t ...` only give a rule's inputs short positional names; they restate no rule.

§ `Test wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      noticeDate IS A DATE
      deadline IS A DATE
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 280(a)(1) Notice to claimants`
`t 280(a)(1) notice` a b noticeDate deadline d e f MEANS
    `s 280(a)(1) Notice to claimants` WITH `statement that claims must be presented in writing with sufficient information reasonably to inform of the identity of the claimant and the substance of the claim` IS a, `statement of the mailing address to which a claim must be sent` IS b, `date of the notice` IS noticeDate, `date by which a claim must be received` IS deadline, `statement that the claim will be barred if not received by that date` IS d, `statement that distributions may be made to other claimants and the stockholders without further notice to the claimant` IS e, `statement of the aggregate amount, on an annual basis, of all distributions to stockholders for each of the 3 years before dissolution` IS f

GIVEN weeks IS A NUMBER
      agentCounty IS A BOOLEAN
      principalPlace IS A BOOLEAN
      assets IS A NUMBER
      national IS A BOOLEAN
      firstPublished IS A DATE
      mailed IS A MAYBE DATE
      toEach IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t 280(a)(1) publication` weeks agentCounty principalPlace assets national firstPublished mailed toEach MEANS
    `s 280(a)(1) the notice to claimants was published and mailed as the paragraph requires` WITH `the number of consecutive weeks in which the notice was published at least once a week` IS weeks, `the notice was published in a newspaper of general circulation in the county in which the office of the corporation's last registered agent in this State is located` IS agentCounty, `the notice was published in a newspaper of general circulation in the corporation's principal place of business` IS principalPlace, `the total assets of the corporation at the time of its dissolution, in dollars` IS assets, `the notice was published at least once in all editions of a daily newspaper with a national circulation` IS national, `the date of the first publication of the notice` IS firstPublished, `the date a copy of the notice was mailed by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested, to each known claimant` IS mailed, `the copy was mailed to each known claimant including persons with claims asserted in a pending action, suit or proceeding to which the corporation is a party` IS toEach

GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
      states IS A BOOLEAN
      copy IS A BOOLEAN
      byReceiver IS A BOOLEAN
      copies295 IS A BOOLEAN
      copy114 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t 280(a)(3) rejection notice` kind states copy byReceiver copies295 copy114 MEANS
    `s 280(a)(3) the notice of rejection states and encloses what the paragraph requires` WITH `the kind of corporation` IS kind, `the notice states that any claim rejected will be barred if an action, suit or proceeding on the claim is not commenced within 120 days of the date of the notice` IS states, `the notice is accompanied by a copy of sections 278 to 283` IS copy, `the notice is sent by a court-appointed receiver or trustee and a claim has been filed under section 295` IS byReceiver, `the notice is accompanied by copies of sections 295 and 296` IS copies295, `the notice is accompanied by a copy of section 114` IS copy114

GIVEN followed IS A BOOLEAN
      madeNotRejected IS A BOOLEAN
      securityOffered IS A BOOLEAN
      securityOrdered IS A BOOLEAN
      matureKnown IS A BOOLEAN
      finallyDetermined IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`t 281(a) must pay` followed madeNotRejected securityOffered securityOrdered matureKnown finallyDetermined MEANS
    `s 281(a) the corporation or successor entity must pay the claim or post the security` WITH `the corporation or successor entity has followed the procedures described in section 280` IS followed, `the claim was made and not rejected in accordance with section 280(a)` IS madeNotRejected, `security was offered and not rejected pursuant to section 280(b)(2)` IS securityOffered, `security was ordered by the Court of Chancery in a proceeding under section 280(c)` IS securityOrdered, `the claim is mature, known and uncontested` IS matureKnown, `the claim has been finally determined to be owing by the corporation or successor entity` IS finallyDetermined

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 281(b) Plan of distribution`
`t 281(b) plan` a b c d e f MEANS
    `s 281(b) Plan of distribution` WITH `provision to pay or make reasonable provision to pay all claims and obligations, including known contingent, conditional or unmatured contractual claims` IS a, `provision reasonably likely to be sufficient for claims in pending actions, suits or proceedings to which the corporation is a party` IS b, `provision reasonably likely to be sufficient for claims likely to arise or become known within 10 years after the date of dissolution` IS c, `provision that the claims be paid in full if there are sufficient assets` IS d, `provision that, if the assets are insufficient, the claims be paid according to their priority and, among claims of equal priority, ratably` IS e, `provision that any remaining assets be distributed to the stockholders` IS f

§ `s 278 Continuation of corporation after dissolution`

-- 3 years.
#ASSERT (`s 278 the term of continuation`)'s `how many units` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`s 278 the term of continuation`)'s unit EQUALS `calendar years`
-- Dissolved 10 March 2026: 3 years run to 10 March 2029.
#ASSERT (`s 278 the last day of the period of continuation` WITH `the date the corporation expired by its own limitation or was dissolved` IS YMD 2026 3 10, `the date to which the Court of Chancery has directed the corporation to be continued, if it has` IS NOTHING) EQUALS YMD 2029 3 10
-- A longer period directed by the Court of Chancery (to 1 January 2031) governs.
#ASSERT (`s 278 the last day of the period of continuation` WITH `the date the corporation expired by its own limitation or was dissolved` IS YMD 2026 3 10, `the date to which the Court of Chancery has directed the corporation to be continued, if it has` IS JUST (YMD 2031 1 1)) EQUALS YMD 2031 1 1
-- A date directed that is not longer than 3 years leaves the 3 years.
#ASSERT (`s 278 the last day of the period of continuation` WITH `the date the corporation expired by its own limitation or was dissolved` IS YMD 2026 3 10, `the date to which the Court of Chancery has directed the corporation to be continued, if it has` IS JUST (YMD 2028 1 1)) EQUALS YMD 2029 3 10
-- Dissolved on 29 February 2024: the 3rd anniversary clamps to 28 February 2027 (the core's reading, fork F2 of the core).
#ASSERT (`s 278 the last day of the period of continuation` WITH `the date the corporation expired by its own limitation or was dissolved` IS YMD 2024 2 29, `the date to which the Court of Chancery has directed the corporation to be continued, if it has` IS NOTHING) EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28
-- The corporation continues for the purposes the text lists, through the last day, and not after.
#ASSERT `s 278 the corporation continues as a body corporate for the purpose` WITH `the purpose` IS `prosecuting and defending suits, whether civil, criminal or administrative, by or against the corporation`, `the date of the question` IS YMD 2029 3 10, `the last day of the period of continuation` IS YMD 2029 3 10
#ASSERT NOT (`s 278 the corporation continues as a body corporate for the purpose` WITH `the purpose` IS `prosecuting and defending suits, whether civil, criminal or administrative, by or against the corporation`, `the date of the question` IS YMD 2029 3 11, `the last day of the period of continuation` IS YMD 2029 3 10)
#ASSERT `s 278 the corporation continues as a body corporate for the purpose` WITH `the purpose` IS `enabling the corporation gradually to settle and close its business`, `the date of the question` IS YMD 2027 1 1, `the last day of the period of continuation` IS YMD 2029 3 10
#ASSERT `s 278 the corporation continues as a body corporate for the purpose` WITH `the purpose` IS `disposing of and conveying its property`, `the date of the question` IS YMD 2027 1 1, `the last day of the period of continuation` IS YMD 2029 3 10
#ASSERT `s 278 the corporation continues as a body corporate for the purpose` WITH `the purpose` IS `discharging its liabilities`, `the date of the question` IS YMD 2027 1 1, `the last day of the period of continuation` IS YMD 2029 3 10
#ASSERT `s 278 the corporation continues as a body corporate for the purpose` WITH `the purpose` IS `distributing to its stockholders any remaining assets`, `the date of the question` IS YMD 2027 1 1, `the last day of the period of continuation` IS YMD 2029 3 10
-- "but not for the purpose of continuing the business for which the corporation was organized": never.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 278 the corporation continues as a body corporate for the purpose` WITH `the purpose` IS `continuing the business for which the corporation was organized`, `the date of the question` IS YMD 2027 1 1, `the last day of the period of continuation` IS YMD 2029 3 10)
-- An action begun in time continues beyond the 3 years until the judgments are fully executed.
#ASSERT `s 278 the corporation continues as a body corporate, and the action does not abate, for the sake of the action, suit or proceeding` WITH `the action, suit or proceeding was begun by or against the corporation prior to, or within 3 years after, the date of its expiration or dissolution` IS TRUE, `the judgments, orders or decrees in the action, suit or proceeding have been fully executed` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 278 the corporation continues as a body corporate, and the action does not abate, for the sake of the action, suit or proceeding` WITH `the action, suit or proceeding was begun by or against the corporation prior to, or within 3 years after, the date of its expiration or dissolution` IS TRUE, `the judgments, orders or decrees in the action, suit or proceeding have been fully executed` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 278 the corporation continues as a body corporate, and the action does not abate, for the sake of the action, suit or proceeding` WITH `the action, suit or proceeding was begun by or against the corporation prior to, or within 3 years after, the date of its expiration or dissolution` IS FALSE, `the judgments, orders or decrees in the action, suit or proceeding have been fully executed` IS FALSE)
-- Sections 279 to 282 apply to a dissolved corporation and to one that expired by its own limitation.
#ASSERT `s 278 sections 279 to 282 apply to the corporation as a dissolved corporation` WITH `the corporation has been dissolved` IS TRUE, `the corporation has expired by its own limitation` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 278 sections 279 to 282 apply to the corporation as a dissolved corporation` WITH `the corporation has been dissolved` IS FALSE, `the corporation has expired by its own limitation` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 278 sections 279 to 282 apply to the corporation as a dissolved corporation` WITH `the corporation has been dissolved` IS FALSE, `the corporation has expired by its own limitation` IS FALSE)

§ `s 279 Trustees or receivers for dissolved corporations`

-- A creditor, a stockholder or a director of a dissolved corporation needs no showing of good cause.
#ASSERT `s 279 the Court of Chancery may act on the application to appoint trustees or receivers` WITH `the corporation organized under this chapter has been dissolved in any manner whatever` IS TRUE, `the applicant` IS `a creditor`, `the applicant shows good cause` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 279 the Court of Chancery may act on the application to appoint trustees or receivers` WITH `the corporation organized under this chapter has been dissolved in any manner whatever` IS TRUE, `the applicant` IS `a stockholder`, `the applicant shows good cause` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 279 the Court of Chancery may act on the application to appoint trustees or receivers` WITH `the corporation organized under this chapter has been dissolved in any manner whatever` IS TRUE, `the applicant` IS `a director`, `the applicant shows good cause` IS FALSE
-- "any other person who shows good cause therefor": an officer, or a party named in the provision, must show it.
#ASSERT `s 279 the Court of Chancery may act on the application to appoint trustees or receivers` WITH `the corporation organized under this chapter has been dissolved in any manner whatever` IS TRUE, `the applicant` IS `an officer`, `the applicant shows good cause` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 279 the Court of Chancery may act on the application to appoint trustees or receivers` WITH `the corporation organized under this chapter has been dissolved in any manner whatever` IS TRUE, `the applicant` IS `an officer`, `the applicant shows good cause` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 279 the Court of Chancery may act on the application to appoint trustees or receivers` WITH `the corporation organized under this chapter has been dissolved in any manner whatever` IS TRUE, `the applicant` IS `another party named in the provision` "a lender to the corporation", `the applicant shows good cause` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 279 the Court of Chancery may act on the application to appoint trustees or receivers` WITH `the corporation organized under this chapter has been dissolved in any manner whatever` IS TRUE, `the applicant` IS `another party named in the provision` "a lender to the corporation", `the applicant shows good cause` IS FALSE)
-- The corporation must have been dissolved.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 279 the Court of Chancery may act on the application to appoint trustees or receivers` WITH `the corporation organized under this chapter has been dissolved in any manner whatever` IS FALSE, `the applicant` IS `a creditor`, `the applicant shows good cause` IS TRUE)
-- A trustee is a director; a receiver is any person; any other office is not covered.
#ASSERT (`s 279 the person may be appointed to the office` WITH `the office` IS `a trustee`, `the appointee is a director of the corporation` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 279 the person may be appointed to the office` WITH `the office` IS `a trustee`, `the appointee is a director of the corporation` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 279 the person may be appointed to the office` WITH `the office` IS `a receiver`, `the appointee is a director of the corporation` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 279 the person may be appointed to the office` WITH `the office` IS `a custodian`, `the appointee is a director of the corporation` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The five powers.
#ASSERT `s 279 the trustee or receiver has the power` WITH `the power` IS `to take charge of the corporation's property`
#ASSERT `s 279 the trustee or receiver has the power` WITH `the power` IS `to collect the debts and property due and belonging to the corporation`
#ASSERT `s 279 the trustee or receiver has the power` WITH `the power` IS `to prosecute and defend, in the name of the corporation or otherwise, all suits necessary or proper for those purposes`
#ASSERT `s 279 the trustee or receiver has the power` WITH `the power` IS `to appoint an agent or agents under them`
#ASSERT `s 279 the trustee or receiver has the power` WITH `the power` IS `to do all other acts which might be done by the corporation, if in being, that may be necessary for the final settlement of its unfinished business`
#ASSERT (count `s 279 the powers of the trustees or receivers`) EQUALS 5
-- The powers continue as long as the Court thinks necessary.
#ASSERT `s 279 the powers of the trustees or receivers may be continued` WITH `the Court of Chancery thinks the continuation of the powers necessary for the purposes` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 279 the powers of the trustees or receivers may be continued` WITH `the Court of Chancery thinks the continuation of the powers necessary for the purposes` IS FALSE)

§ `s 280 Notice to claimants; filing of claims`

§§ `s 280(a)(1) the notice`

-- 60 days.
#ASSERT (`s 280(a)(1) the least time allowed to present a claim`)'s `how many units` EQUALS 60
#ASSERT (`s 280(a)(1) the least time allowed to present a claim`)'s unit EQUALS `calendar days`
-- Notice dated 1 June 2026: a date to receive claims "no earlier than 60 days from the date thereof" is 31 July 2026 or later.
--  columns: (a.) writing, (b.) address, date of the notice, date claims must be received, (d.) barred, (e.) distributions, (f.) annual amounts
#ASSERT `s 280(a)(1) the notice to claimants states what the paragraph requires` WITH `the notice` IS (`t 280(a)(1) notice` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 7 31) TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 280(a)(1) the notice to claimants states what the paragraph requires` WITH `the notice` IS (`t 280(a)(1) notice` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 7 30) TRUE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT `s 280(a)(1) the notice to claimants states what the paragraph requires` WITH `the notice` IS (`t 280(a)(1) notice` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 8 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 280(a)(1) the notice to claimants states what the paragraph requires` WITH `the notice` IS (`t 280(a)(1) notice` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 8 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 280(a)(1) the notice to claimants states what the paragraph requires` WITH `the notice` IS (`t 280(a)(1) notice` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 8 15) TRUE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 280(a)(1) the notice to claimants states what the paragraph requires` WITH `the notice` IS (`t 280(a)(1) notice` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 8 15) FALSE TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 280(a)(1) the notice to claimants states what the paragraph requires` WITH `the notice` IS (`t 280(a)(1) notice` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 8 15) TRUE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 280(a)(1) the notice to claimants states what the paragraph requires` WITH `the notice` IS (`t 280(a)(1) notice` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 8 15) TRUE TRUE FALSE))
-- $10,000,000.
#ASSERT `s 280(a)(1) the total assets from which a national daily newspaper is required` EQUALS 10000000
-- Publication: 2 consecutive weeks, in the agent's county and the principal place of business; mailing on or before the first publication.
--  columns: weeks, agent's county, principal place, total assets, national daily, first publication, date mailed, mailed to each known claimant
#ASSERT `t 280(a)(1) publication` 2 TRUE TRUE 5000000 FALSE (YMD 2026 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)) TRUE
#ASSERT `t 280(a)(1) publication` 3 TRUE TRUE 5000000 FALSE (YMD 2026 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 9)) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`t 280(a)(1) publication` 1 TRUE TRUE 5000000 FALSE (YMD 2026 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`t 280(a)(1) publication` 2 FALSE TRUE 5000000 FALSE (YMD 2026 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`t 280(a)(1) publication` 2 TRUE FALSE 5000000 FALSE (YMD 2026 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)) TRUE)
-- Assets of $9,999,999: no national daily newspaper needed; $10,000,000: needed.
#ASSERT `t 280(a)(1) publication` 2 TRUE TRUE 9999999 FALSE (YMD 2026 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`t 280(a)(1) publication` 2 TRUE TRUE 10000000 FALSE (YMD 2026 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)) TRUE)
#ASSERT `t 280(a)(1) publication` 2 TRUE TRUE 10000000 TRUE (YMD 2026 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)) TRUE
-- The copy mailed one day after the first publication is too late; none mailed, or not to each known claimant, fails.
#ASSERT NOT (`t 280(a)(1) publication` 2 TRUE TRUE 5000000 FALSE (YMD 2026 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 11)) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`t 280(a)(1) publication` 2 TRUE TRUE 5000000 FALSE (YMD 2026 6 10) NOTHING TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`t 280(a)(1) publication` 2 TRUE TRUE 5000000 FALSE (YMD 2026 6 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 10)) FALSE)

§§ `s 280(a)(2) to (a)(4) bars`

-- (a)(2): the claimant was given actual notice and presented the claim on the date claims were to be received: not barred.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 280(a)(2) the claim is barred for want of presentation` WITH `the claim is one required to be presented under subsection (a), that is, not a claim in a pending action, suit or proceeding to which the corporation is a party` IS TRUE, `the claimant was given actual notice under subsection (a)` IS TRUE, `the date the claim was presented to the dissolved corporation or successor entity, if it was` IS JUST (YMD 2026 7 31), `the date by which a claim must be received, as the notice states` IS YMD 2026 7 31)
-- One day after: barred.
#ASSERT `s 280(a)(2) the claim is barred for want of presentation` WITH `the claim is one required to be presented under subsection (a), that is, not a claim in a pending action, suit or proceeding to which the corporation is a party` IS TRUE, `the claimant was given actual notice under subsection (a)` IS TRUE, `the date the claim was presented to the dissolved corporation or successor entity, if it was` IS JUST (YMD 2026 8 1), `the date by which a claim must be received, as the notice states` IS YMD 2026 7 31
-- Never presented: barred.
#ASSERT `s 280(a)(2) the claim is barred for want of presentation` WITH `the claim is one required to be presented under subsection (a), that is, not a claim in a pending action, suit or proceeding to which the corporation is a party` IS TRUE, `the claimant was given actual notice under subsection (a)` IS TRUE, `the date the claim was presented to the dissolved corporation or successor entity, if it was` IS NOTHING, `the date by which a claim must be received, as the notice states` IS YMD 2026 7 31
-- No actual notice: not barred by this paragraph. A claim in a pending action: not one required to be presented.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 280(a)(2) the claim is barred for want of presentation` WITH `the claim is one required to be presented under subsection (a), that is, not a claim in a pending action, suit or proceeding to which the corporation is a party` IS TRUE, `the claimant was given actual notice under subsection (a)` IS FALSE, `the date the claim was presented to the dissolved corporation or successor entity, if it was` IS NOTHING, `the date by which a claim must be received, as the notice states` IS YMD 2026 7 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 280(a)(2) the claim is barred for want of presentation` WITH `the claim is one required to be presented under subsection (a), that is, not a claim in a pending action, suit or proceeding to which the corporation is a party` IS FALSE, `the claimant was given actual notice under subsection (a)` IS TRUE, `the date the claim was presented to the dissolved corporation or successor entity, if it was` IS NOTHING, `the date by which a claim must be received, as the notice states` IS YMD 2026 7 31)
-- 90 days and 150 days.
#ASSERT (`s 280(a)(3) the longest time after receipt of a claim to mail the rejection`)'s `how many units` EQUALS 90
#ASSERT (`s 280(a)(3) the least time before the end of the period of continuation to mail the rejection`)'s `how many units` EQUALS 150
-- (a)(3): claim received 1 March 2026, the period ends 1 January 2028. 90 days after receipt is 30 May 2026.
#ASSERT (`s 280(a)(3) the rejection was mailed in time` WITH `the claim was filed under section 295 against a corporation or successor entity for which a receiver or trustee has been appointed by the Court of Chancery` IS FALSE, `the date the claim was received` IS YMD 2026 3 1, `the date the rejection notice was mailed by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested` IS YMD 2026 5 30, `the last day of the period described in section 278` IS YMD 2028 1 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 280(a)(3) the rejection was mailed in time` WITH `the claim was filed under section 295 against a corporation or successor entity for which a receiver or trustee has been appointed by the Court of Chancery` IS FALSE, `the date the claim was received` IS YMD 2026 3 1, `the date the rejection notice was mailed by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested` IS YMD 2026 5 31, `the last day of the period described in section 278` IS YMD 2028 1 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "and, in all events, at least 150 days before the expiration": claim received 1 June 2027 (90 days later is 30 August 2027), but 150 days before 1 January 2028 is 4 August 2027.
#ASSERT (`s 280(a)(3) the rejection was mailed in time` WITH `the claim was filed under section 295 against a corporation or successor entity for which a receiver or trustee has been appointed by the Court of Chancery` IS FALSE, `the date the claim was received` IS YMD 2027 6 1, `the date the rejection notice was mailed by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested` IS YMD 2027 8 4, `the last day of the period described in section 278` IS YMD 2028 1 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 280(a)(3) the rejection was mailed in time` WITH `the claim was filed under section 295 against a corporation or successor entity for which a receiver or trustee has been appointed by the Court of Chancery` IS FALSE, `the date the claim was received` IS YMD 2027 6 1, `the date the rejection notice was mailed by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested` IS YMD 2027 8 5, `the last day of the period described in section 278` IS YMD 2028 1 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A claim filed under section 295 where a receiver or trustee has been appointed: section 296 governs, so not covered here.
#ASSERT (`s 280(a)(3) the rejection was mailed in time` WITH `the claim was filed under section 295 against a corporation or successor entity for which a receiver or trustee has been appointed by the Court of Chancery` IS TRUE, `the date the claim was received` IS YMD 2026 3 1, `the date the rejection notice was mailed by certified or registered mail, return receipt requested` IS YMD 2026 5 30, `the last day of the period described in section 278` IS YMD 2028 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The notice of rejection.
--  columns: kind, states the 120-day bar, copy of sections 278-283, sent by a receiver or trustee on a section 295 claim, copies of sections 295 and 296, copy of section 114
#ASSERT `t 280(a)(3) rejection notice` `a stock corporation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`t 280(a)(3) rejection notice` `a stock corporation` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`t 280(a)(3) rejection notice` `a stock corporation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`t 280(a)(3) rejection notice` `a stock corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `t 280(a)(3) rejection notice` `a stock corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Subsection (g): the notice of a nonstock corporation also includes a copy of section 114.
#ASSERT NOT (`t 280(a)(3) rejection notice` `a charitable nonstock corporation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `t 280(a)(3) rejection notice` `a charitable nonstock corporation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`t 280(a)(3) rejection notice` `a nonstock corporation with membership interests` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`t 280(a)(3) rejection notice` `a nonprofit nonstock corporation that is not charitable` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- (a)(4): rejection notice mailed 1 June 2026; 120 days later is 29 September 2026.
#ASSERT (`s 280(a)(4) the longest time after the mailing of the rejection notice to commence an action`)'s `how many units` EQUALS 120
#ASSERT NOT (`s 280(a)(4) the claim is barred for want of an action after the rejection` WITH `the claim was rejected pursuant to paragraph (a)(3)` IS TRUE, `the date the rejection notice was mailed` IS YMD 2026 6 1, `the date the claimant commenced an action, suit or proceeding on the claim, if the claimant did` IS JUST (YMD 2026 9 29))
#ASSERT `s 280(a)(4) the claim is barred for want of an action after the rejection` WITH `the claim was rejected pursuant to paragraph (a)(3)` IS TRUE, `the date the rejection notice was mailed` IS YMD 2026 6 1, `the date the claimant commenced an action, suit or proceeding on the claim, if the claimant did` IS JUST (YMD 2026 9 30)
#ASSERT `s 280(a)(4) the claim is barred for want of an action after the rejection` WITH `the claim was rejected pursuant to paragraph (a)(3)` IS TRUE, `the date the rejection notice was mailed` IS YMD 2026 6 1, `the date the claimant commenced an action, suit or proceeding on the claim, if the claimant did` IS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`s 280(a)(4) the claim is barred for want of an action after the rejection` WITH `the claim was rejected pursuant to paragraph (a)(3)` IS FALSE, `the date the rejection notice was mailed` IS YMD 2026 6 1, `the date the claimant commenced an action, suit or proceeding on the claim, if the claimant did` IS NOTHING)

§§ `s 280(b) contractual claims`

-- A contingent contractual claim is a contractual claim; an implied warranty on a product is not.
#ASSERT `s 280(b)(1) the claim is a contractual claim for the purposes of sections 280 and 281` WITH `the claim is a contractual claim contingent upon the occurrence or nonoccurrence of future events or otherwise conditional or unmatured` IS TRUE, `the claim is an implied warranty as to a product manufactured, sold, distributed or handled by the dissolved corporation` IS FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 280(b)(1) the claim is a contractual claim for the purposes of sections 280 and 281` WITH `the claim is a contractual claim contingent upon the occurrence or nonoccurrence of future events or otherwise conditional or unmatured` IS TRUE, `the claim is an implied warranty as to a product manufactured, sold, distributed or handled by the dissolved corporation` IS TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 280(b)(1) the claim is a contractual claim for the purposes of sections 280 and 281` WITH `the claim is a contractual claim contingent upon the occurrence or nonoccurrence of future events or otherwise conditional or unmatured` IS FALSE, `the claim is an implied warranty as to a product manufactured, sold, distributed or handled by the dissolved corporation` IS FALSE)
-- The notice the corporation must also give such a person.
#ASSERT `s 280(b)(1) the corporation has given the person with a contractual claim the notice it must also give` WITH `the corporation or successor entity elects to follow the procedures described in subsection (a)` IS TRUE, `the person has a contractual claim within the meaning of section 280(b)(1)` IS TRUE, `the notice to the person is in substantially the form of the notice described in paragraph (a)(1)` IS TRUE, `the notice to the person is sent and published in the same manner as the notice described in paragraph (a)(1)` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 280(b)(1) the corporation has given the person with a contractual claim the notice it must also give` WITH `the corporation or successor entity elects to follow the procedures described in subsection (a)` IS FALSE, `the person has a contractual claim within the meaning of section 280(b)(1)` IS TRUE, `the notice to the person is in substantially the form of the notice described in paragraph (a)(1)` IS TRUE, `the notice to the person is sent and published in the same manner as the notice described in paragraph (a)(1)` IS TRUE)
