#ASSERT NOT (`s 280(c)(2) the corporation or successor entity must petition the Court of Chancery to determine the security for the claimant who rejected the offer` WITH `the corporation or successor entity has given notice in accordance with subsections (a) and (b)` IS TRUE, `the claimant has rejected the offer for security made pursuant to paragraph (b)(2)` IS FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 280(c)(3) the corporation or successor entity must petition the Court of Chancery to determine the security for claims not yet made known` WITH `the corporation or successor entity has given notice in accordance with subsection (a)` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 280(c)(3) the corporation or successor entity must petition the Court of Chancery to determine the security for claims not yet made known` WITH `the corporation or successor entity has given notice in accordance with subsection (a)` IS FALSE)
-- Claims likely to arise within 5 years after dissolution on 10 March 2026, or a longer period the Court determines up to 10 years.
#ASSERT (`s 280(c)(3) the last day of the period within which claims likely to arise are provided for` WITH `the date of dissolution` IS YMD 2026 3 10, `the last day of the longer period the Court of Chancery has determined, if it has` IS NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2031 3 10)
#ASSERT (`s 280(c)(3) the last day of the period within which claims likely to arise are provided for` WITH `the date of dissolution` IS YMD 2026 3 10, `the last day of the longer period the Court of Chancery has determined, if it has` IS JUST (YMD 2033 3 10)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2033 3 10)
#ASSERT (`s 280(c)(3) the last day of the period within which claims likely to arise are provided for` WITH `the date of dissolution` IS YMD 2026 3 10, `the last day of the longer period the Court of Chancery has determined, if it has` IS JUST (YMD 2036 3 10)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2036 3 10)
-- More than 10 years: the text does not allow it.
#ASSERT (`s 280(c)(3) the last day of the period within which claims likely to arise are provided for` WITH `the date of dissolution` IS YMD 2026 3 10, `the last day of the longer period the Court of Chancery has determined, if it has` IS JUST (YMD 2036 3 11)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A "longer period" that is shorter than 5 years is not longer: 5 years stands.
#ASSERT (`s 280(c)(3) the last day of the period within which claims likely to arise are provided for` WITH `the date of dissolution` IS YMD 2026 3 10, `the last day of the longer period the Court of Chancery has determined, if it has` IS JUST (YMD 2029 1 1)) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2031 3 10)
