#ASSERT NOT (`s 284 a proceeding to revoke or forfeit the charter may be instituted` WITH `the Attorney General proceeds by complaint in the Court of Chancery` IS FALSE, `the ground` IS `abuse of its corporate powers, privileges or franchises`, `the date the corporation was incorporated` IS YMD 2024 5 1, `the date the proceeding is instituted` IS YMD 2026 5 1)
-- (b): after a revocation or forfeiture by the Court, it may administer and wind up the affairs.
#ASSERT `s 284(b) the Court of Chancery has power to administer and wind up the affairs of the corporation and to make the orders and decrees just and equitable respecting its affairs and assets and the rights of its stockholders and creditors` WITH `the charter of the corporation has been revoked or forfeited by the Court of Chancery under section 284` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 284(b) the Court of Chancery has power to administer and wind up the affairs of the corporation and to make the orders and decrees just and equitable respecting its affairs and assets and the rights of its stockholders and creditors` WITH `the charter of the corporation has been revoked or forfeited by the Court of Chancery under section 284` IS FALSE)
-- Section 285: a decree dissolving the corporation or forfeiting the charter is filed with the Secretary of State and noted.
#ASSERT `s 285 the decree or judgment must be filed in the office of the Secretary of State and noted on the charter and the index` WITH `the corporation has been dissolved or its charter forfeited by decree or judgment of the Court of Chancery` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 285 the decree or judgment must be filed in the office of the Secretary of State and noted on the charter and the index` WITH `the corporation has been dissolved or its charter forfeited by decree or judgment of the Court of Chancery` IS FALSE)
